  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Quality Instruction Toward Access and Basic Education Improvement (QITABI 3)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Lebanon):  USAID will continue to support Lebanon&apos;s education sector to improve student learning outcomes across Lebanon&apos;s 1,200 public schools and in select low-cost private schools that cater for vulnerable and economically disadvantaged populations. Through the Quality Instruction Toward Access and Basic Education Improvement (QITABI 3) activity, USAID will ensure that children and youth receive improved instruction resulting in gains in literacy, numeracy, and social and emotional skills, and that higher proportions of students&apos; complete school. QITABI 3 will work closely with the Ministry of Education and Higher Education (MEHE) and the Center for Educational Research and Development (CERD) to improve their institutional effectiveness to deliver quality educational services, accelerating the Ministry&apos;s education reform agenda, and developing systems that achieve maximum impact in providing quality education. FY 2024 assistance will provide teaching and learning materials and equipment to schools; support evidence-based teaching methods, develop assessment tools; implement youth initiatives; and provide training to teachers and educators in reading pedagogy, numeracy, and social and emotional learning skills so that both teachers and students are empowered to foster an environment where education is accessible, inclusive, and transformative. QITABI 3 is attributed to the basic education earmark. The directive pertaining to girls in areas of conflict will be fully met through this activity...</narrative>
  </description>
